     1	# APPROACHES.md — current research strategy
     2	
     3	Updated 2026-09-06 through12:03Z against the coordinator handoff and later
     4	entries in `AUDIT.md`. This is a strategy
     5	map, not a proof or promotion record. Live
     6	owners and jobs belong in the newest `LIVE STATE` in `notes.md`.
     7	
     8	## What the campaign has established
     9	
    10	The reviewed census-coverage theorem supplies necessary conditions for
    11	normalized minimal counterexamples at arbitrary degree. The enumerated
    12	window is still finite: at n <= 200 the accepted chain is 24,063 census rows
    13	-> 90 actual-stabilizer rows -> 64 residual necessary configurations.
    14	Those 64 consist of 44 u_s = 1 rows and 20 u_s >= 2 rows. They are not
    15	polynomial pairs. See `AUDIT.md`, 17(ccccccccc), 17(ggggggggggg), and the
    16	dated 2026-09-06T04:03Z state.
    17	
    18	Internal (99,66) and D=108 computations remain undecided; earlier internal
    19	closure announcements were superseded by support/radius/stratum corrections.
    20	But the external GGHV degree99 exclusion now puts new99 frontier work on HOLD
    21	pending its primary-source applicability gate (see below). These are different
    22	evidence layers, not competing definitions of an open mathematical problem.
    23	The K16 theorem (T) is promoted only for t <= 8. Neither this finite range
    24	nor excluding the whole K16 ray would by itself resolve plane JC2.
    25	
    26	## Current proof fronts
    27	
    28	| Front | Accepted reduction / useful object | Remaining obligation |
    29	|---|---|---|
    30	| u_s = 1 receivers | Licensed Moh descent, with the child's own characteristic data and full source support | Exclude the necessary polynomial receivers uniformly, or find a structural descent that strictly improves an invariant. The 44 rows are only the n <= 200 test population. |
    31	| Split branches | Corrected two-point systems; characteristic-degree attainment; direct T2+T3 compression under review | Prove the source-to-chart implication, then decide the full necessary system. The 20 class-C rows, (99,66) split branches, and D=108 are clients, not an all-degree finite classification. |
    32	| K16 prototype | Whole-polynomial equation (UF), reconstructed ideals K_m, and the terminal target B*eta | A uniform argument on the required nonzero-product locus, plus the separate b = 0 boundary. All coefficient-field factors and actual degrees must be covered. |
    33	
    34	The general proof needs exclusion of every datum supplied by the coverage
    35	theorem, without an unproved degree, support, depth, or height cap. A source
    36	row sharing numerical parameters with a solved receiver does not inherit its
    37	certificate without a proved map. Keep an explicit unassigned branch when a
    38	receiver map has not been established.
    39	
    40	### Counterexample front: full-ideal properness
    41	
    42	The completed [different-model gate](xmodel/full-ideal-counterexample-gate-fable5-20260906.md)
    43	confirms that every point of the COMPLETE direct ideal reconstructs polynomials
    44	of degrees (99,66) or (108,72) with nonzero constant Jacobian. The one-way
    45	implication is promoted with the corrections in `AUDIT.md` 17(ppppppppppp).
    46	Exact properness would give a counterexample by Nullstellensatz and
    47	plane-automorphism degree divisibility; explicit coordinates or a canonical
    48	resultant lift would not be logically required. NO PROPERNESS IS KNOWN.
    49	
    50	This does not apply to the live 466-row proper-subset solve, modular points,
    51	or truncated survivors. The frozen full builder has a completion-count
    52	assertion bug; its executable output needs separate repair/validation.
    53	The gate's suggestion to discard `t3eq` as rowless is wrong and is not
    54	adopted. A subset unit excludes the full chart; excluding a source
    55	configuration still needs the unproved source-to-chart interface.
    56	
    57	The [nonemptiness pilot](xmodel/nonemptiness-certificate-astra-20260906.md)
    58	specifies a smaller acceptance certificate: exact coordinates in a nonzero
    59	finite Q-algebra, checked against every full row through the circuit. It
    60	has no candidate. A smooth mod-p subsystem alone does not certify a lift.
    61	The recovered all-degree characteristic-tower analogue is now independently
    62	reviewed, with exact hypotheses in AUDIT 17(sssssssssss). It is recovery of
    63	an old appendix, not an existence or exclusion result. The review's proposed
    64	T3 replacement is not automatically equivalent on every D108 T2 chart, nor
    65	quadratic in the current nonlinear semantic coordinates.
    66	
    67	### Parent-residue pilot
    68	
    69	The [R050 local calculation](xmodel/r050-parent-residue-pilot-astra-20260906.md)
    70	extracts four generic-fibre residue coefficients at the physical ramification-4
    71	place. The independent review confirms its scoped mathematics, with root's
    72	larger replay still pending; it is not yet promoted. The constraint
    73	is independent of three specified faces but already implied by the full
    74	Jacobian equations. Test actual early pruning before scaling to other rows;
    75	there is no R050 exclusion, and fibrewise exactness does not supply a global
    76	polynomial mate.
    77	
    78	### K16: use the conclusion the terminal chart consumes
    79	
    80	The current U_eta proposal asks for eta_m = 0 on V(K_m) with b != 0.
    81	The recorded implication chain actually consumes B_m*eta_m = 0 there.
    82	Consequently a sufficient, weaker open-chart target is
    83	
    84	```text
    85	For every actual m >= 4 and every factor of Q[d]/(3d^2-m),
    86	V(K_m) has no geometric point with b*B_m*eta_m != 0.
    87	```
    88	
    89	This is a coordinator target selection, not a new exclusion theorem.
    90	It follows from the existing specialization/terminal-target chain in
    91	[the whole-polynomial report](xmodel/k16-ueta-classification-astra-20260906.md),
    92	section 8. The product target itself was already explicit in
    93	[the earlier Abel report](xmodel/k16-f3abel-astra-20260905.md); this restores
    94	that target rather than claiming a new mathematical mechanism.
    95	
    96	The same report's SUPPORT argument says B != 0 forces support gcd 1.
    97	Thus the B = 0 parity families need no exclusion for this product target.
    98	The b = 0 boundary remains an independent obligation. Full classification
    99	of all polynomial solutions is stronger than the conclusion currently needed.
   100	THICK rules out a fixed nilpotence exponent; it does not rule out a proved
   101	formula whose exponent grows with the parameter.
   102	
   103	The [reviewed boundary lemma](xmodel/k16-boundary-product-gate-fable5-20260906.md)
   104	now returns marked rational solutions to polynomials when B!=0, and an exact
   105	quadratic norm model retains the full differential filter. It does not exclude
   106	polynomial solutions or add an independent equation; the missing all-m
   107	obstruction is unchanged. See AUDIT17(zzzzzzzzzzz).
   108	
   109	### Computational work
   110	
   111	Continue the already-launched capped solves; their
   112	custody and harvest instructions are in the
   113	[handoff](box/HANDOFF-20260906T0840Z-coordinator.md). A longer run can be
   114	justified by measured progress. Increasing RAM alone does not answer a
   115	runtime or elimination-degree wall.
   116	
   117	Judge a representation by expanded terms, elimination degree, matrix growth,
   118	memory, and certificate cost, as well as variable count. The recorded R005
   119	rewrite reduces 53,209,262 terms to 2,902,778 before further pivots, but its
   120	completed continuation found no solver decision. Deeper elimination increased
   121	terms (10.66M at36 pivots;17.85M at54), and the solver timings were not controlled
   122	comparisons. Do not automatically extend it or port it across the44 receivers.
   123	See AUDIT17(wwwwwwwwwww) for proof/control corrections. Prefer reusable
   124	algebraic reductions over another raw chart sweep.
   125	
   126	For exclusion, the essential direction is: every genuine source pair
   127	supplies a solution of the tested necessary chart. Surjectivity back to
   128	source pairs is not needed. A failed reconstruction theorem alone does not
   129	invalidate an emptiness argument whose necessary direction still holds.
   130	Conversely, a necessary-chart point is not a counterexample; reconstruction
   131	and a direct characteristic-zero check of the actual pair are required.
   132	The completed reviews support the scoped T2/T3 mathematics and literal-subset
   133	implication with fixes, but not the frozen full builder's completion claim.
   134	The R005 abstract quotient substitution is valid; its random-point control is
   135	not an exact instance certificate. A bounded factored-
   136	Jacobian pilot has now completed a600-variable/1629-row full physical-J
   137	export in137s/1.71GiB. Its complete encoding is now independently reviewed
   138	and root-replayed at exact all-row scope;
   139	this is a construction advantage, not a measured solver win or T2/T3
   140	equivalence. See AUDIT17(cccccccccccc). The old2TB input build was stopped
   141	after142minutes of construction without a closed stream; all partial artifacts
   142	and the protected machine are retained. A capped solver discriminator on the
   143	complete physical-J ideal timed out without a basis; modular msolve hit a
   144	new allocation-overflow defect. The first24 C substitutions worsened expanded
   145	construction despite reducing the variable count. The189-pivot Opus gate is
   146	terminal; root adjudication of its useful controls and census objections is
   147	pending. A new transverse-line argument gives uniform full-C rank191 and a
   148	desk190-pivot W-filtration lemma, under independent Fable review. Neither
   149	rank nor fewer variables implies a solver win.
