   159	## Exhausted mechanisms and their precise limits
   160	
   161	| Mechanism | What the current record rules out |
   162	|---|---|
   163	| More arithmetic descent on the same conditions | The repaired descent-invariance lemma transports those conditions; it supplies no new exclusions. Child-specific conditions require their own proof. |
   164	| Child integrality in the current window | R063 is excluded; the six disputed family-B rows survive the complete printed test. No further yield at n <= 200 is banked. |
   165	| Descent on class C | The radius hypothesis concerns actual roots and is not supplied by the row's numerical floor. All 20 current rows are unlicensed for this use. |
   166	| Truncated split-band exclusions | The cone-vertex theorem preserves J = 0 solutions below the necessary normalization depth. |
   167	| Attainment leader alone on unsaturated receivers | The x-charge obstruction prevents the proposed lambda-power certificate. Keeping the full nonzero-Jacobian condition returns to the harder system. |
   168	| Constant-exponent K16 radical certificates | THICK forces the exponent to grow with N. Finite examples do not establish an all-N identity. |
   169	| K16 leading-degree balance / free-jet continuation | Leading balance is consistent at every degree; the free coefficient list grows. Neither argument bounds actual degree. |
   170	
   171	A negative result closes its stated mechanism and hypotheses, not every
   172	approach using the same mathematical vocabulary.
