    30	
    31	```text
    32	[x^1]E = B*(eta - w1 - (3/4)c^2),   independent of a0, a1.
    33	```
    34	
    35	This is (PD) with `W'(0)` free, stronger than the checker, which fixes `W'(0)=eta` and reads off `-(3/4)Bc^2`. With `B!=0` and the linear marking, `c=0` and `A` is polynomial. `eta!=0` is not used.
