    57	## Why (99,66) is in scope, not a Laurent/Newton label artifact
    58	
    59	The brief's central distinction is the right one to check, and it resolves
    60	cleanly in favour of applicability.
    61	
    62	GGV's machinery genuinely does live on reduced objects: `L^{(1)} = K[x,x^{-1},y]`
    63	with `[P,Q] = x^2`, Newton polygons with fractional corners, `1/l · Z × N_0`
    64	supports (`REDUCTION.md:482,940–950`; GGV1 introduction, local scan
    65	`core-ggv-layout.txt`). A degree pair read off a *polygon label* in that setting
    66	is not an absolute total degree, and conflating the two would be exactly the
    67	Flag/place/series error FALLACY-v2 warns about.
    68	
    69	But the (99,66) datum is not a polygon label. `full-ideal-counterexample-gate`
    70	Arrow 1 establishes, at **every** point of the semantic affine space and before
    71	any row is imposed, that `h, D, C` are honest elements of `K[x,y]` (support
    72	condition `r+z ≤ N`, no division by a variable), that
    73	`F = h³+(3D+a)h/2+C` and `G = h²−bh/3+D` have **exact** total degrees 99 and 66
    74	(corrections `≤98<99`, `≤65<66`), with parameter-free top forms
    75	`F_top = y^{27}(y−x)^{72}`, `G_top = y^{18}(y−x)^{48}`. Arrow 2 then gives
    76	`J(F,G) ∈ K^×` at every field point, and Arrow 3 pushes a proper ideal to a
    77	`Qbar`-point. `factored-jacobian-gate-fable5:71` independently records
    78	`deg h = 33, deg D = 34, deg C = 35`; `linear-c-transverse-rank-astra:52–54`
    79	independently records `deg G = 66`, `G_top = H^6`, `H = (X+W)^3 W^8` with
    80	`X=x, W=y−x` — the same `y^{18}(y−x)^{48}`. Three charged reports agree.
    81	
    82	These are absolute total degrees of genuine polynomials over a field of
    83	characteristic zero. Minimal-counterexample normalization does not rescue the
    84	configuration either, and this is the step worth being explicit about: the
    85	dichotomy's quantifier is over *all* counterexamples, not over a distinguished
    86	minimal one. Even on the weakest reading — “the minimum over all counterexamples
    87	of `max(deg)` is `≥125` unless the minimizer is `(72,108)`” — an actual
    88	counterexample of degrees (99,66) would witness `max = 99 < 125` and force that
    89	minimum to be `≤99`, contradicting the statement. The same structural point is
    90	already recorded for the sibling invariant: `[[ggv-B-minimum-over-all-counterexamples]]`
    91	notes GGV1 Cor 6.6 defines `B` on p. 2 as the min gcd over **all**
    92	counterexamples, so `gcd ≥ 16` needs no “minimal degree sum minimizes gcd”
    93	claim. A degree dichotomy proved for the reduced/normalized representative
    94	transfers to the absolute pair because the reduction only ever decreases degree.
    95	No normalization escape hatch exists here.
    96	
    97	**No `SCOPE_CONFLICT`.** (99,66) is an ordinary in-scope point of GGV22 §2.
