    31	                                                                                        1     Introduction
    32	                                               The plane Jacobian Conjecture (see [8]) can be rephrased in the following manner:
    33	                                                  If a pair of polynomials (P, Q) in K[x, y] satisfies [P, Q] := Px Qy − Py Qx ∈ K × , then there
    34	                                               exists a polynomial inverse to the morphism (P, Q) : K 2 → K 2 .
    35	                                                  In [10] the author discards all possible counterexamples with max{deg(P ), deg(Q)} ≤ 100
    36	                                               using approximate roots of polynomials in two variables, but provides a detailed proof only for
