+`PRIMARY99_VERDICT=APPLIES_AS_EXTERNAL_THEOREM`. The local 25-page
+arXiv:2204.14178v1 closes `OPEN[PRIMARY-TEXT-UNREAD]`. Theorem 2.1 says that
+*any* counterexample has maximum degree at least 125 or degree pair
+`(72,108)/(108,72)` (paper pp.2–3; `ggvh-2204.14178v1.txt:94-126`). This is not
+restricted to an arbitrary target representative or stated only for a minimal
+normalized pair.
+
+Actual 99 chain: §2 assigns maximum 99 to `A0=(9,24),(m,n)=(2,3)`.
+Proposition 4.2 (pp.7–10; text `:348-491`) sends any such counterexample to one
+of three nonnegative Newton polygons with `[P,Q]=x`, all sharing P endpoints
+`(6,16),(6,18)` and Q endpoints `(9,24),(9,27)`. Theorem 5.1 (pp.14–20;
+text `:657-981`) forbids polynomial pairs with exactly those endpoint data and
+`[P,Q]=x+g(y)`; take `g=0`. Its proof constructs the approximate root, obtains
+a separable degree-six polynomial, polynomializes the `D_k`, eliminates nine
+coefficient equations to (5.9), then contradicts (5.11) for both multiplicity
+branches `k>=8` and `k<=7`. Corollary 5.7 is the separate `(9,27)`/108 branch,
+not the 99 kill.
+
+Independent exact replay here checked the printed ODE solution and
+squarefreeness and reconstructed the nine-equation elimination to (5.9),
+including the `d_-1=0` exceptional case. I did **not** replay Proposition 4.2
+or the exhaustive table imported from [5]. Thus
+`OPEN[DEPENDENCY-PRIMARY-UNREAD]`: cited [1],[2],[3],[5],[6],[12] were not
+charged/read, and the paper prints no CAS transcript. This is a reproduction
+and preprint trust boundary, not a found proof defect. The ledger's orientation
+slip and unrefereed-chain objections concern Proposition 4.3/the surviving
+72/108 route (`AUDIT.md:5394-5414,10219-10264`); the searched record contains
+no specific objection to the 99 chain (`AUDIT.md:18235-18239`).
+
+The complete physical-J gate independently gives genuine polynomials of exact
+degrees 99/66 and point `=>` Keller nonautomorphism
+(`xmodel/factored-jacobian-gate-fable5-20260906.md:163-178`). Hence the external
+theorem empties that *complete* chart; reverse source-to-chart necessity is
+irrelevant. This is not an internally computed unit. Nor does full-ideal unit
+imply the 466-row proper subset is unit; the old Opus prediction at
+`classical99-interface-opus5-20260906.md:150-152` is rejected.
+
+Terminal-gate reconciliation: the factored-J gate confirms reconstruction,
+complete rows and point-to-counterexample only; its cost claim is measured, not
+a solve. The transverse-C gate passes uniform full-C rank 191, the abstract
+maximal-minor left inverse and the 190-pivot desk lemma, while
+`OPEN[POSITIVE-ONLY-C-UNIFORM]`, `OPEN[CONSTANT-191-MINOR]` and
+`OPEN[W-ADAPTED-EMISSION]` remain internal obligations
+(`linear-c-transverse-gate-fable5-20260906.md:171-186`). The K16 gate confirms
+the marked rational-to-polynomial boundary lemma and norm/DF equivalence, but
+the all-m product target remains OPEN and the rewrite adds no equation
+(`k16-boundary-product-gate-fable5-20260906.md:49-75`). Finally, 24 C pivots
+gave no construction win; exact full-J timed out and modular parsing crashed
+before F4, so neither has algebraic force (`AUDIT.md:18217-18227`).
+
+## Bottlenecks and one card
+
+Proof bottleneck: a source-compatible, uniform all-degree realizability
+obstruction. The 24,063→90→64 census is only a finite necessary population,
+not 64 externally open cases. Full-C rank 191/abstract left inverse supplies no
+properness; K16's rational-to-polynomial lemma and norm model supply no
+polynomial nonexistence. CE bottleneck: an actual point/properness certificate
+in a licensed open family; none exists for D108, K16, or any other client.
+
+**Card D108→GGHV `(8,28)` (`NEW` connection; `OPEN[SOURCE-TO-FRONTIER-MAP]`).**
+Mechanism: map the literal D108 source—whose top `h=(X+W)^8W^28`,
+`F_top=h^3,G_top=h^2`—into the surviving Proposition-4.3 branch, declaring
+field, rings, generator order, normalization, and every image/hypothesis.
+Cheapest decisive test: a desk-scale exact map table plus one valid image and
+one deliberately mutated non-image control; no solve. PASS licenses D108 as a
+known-frontier client only, not existence; mismatch kills this port, not D108;
+an unavailable route stays typed OPEN. Stop at the first unmapped hypothesis;
+no AWS, heavy CAS, or 99-code analogy. Strongest falsification is that identical
+`(8,28)` top data need not identify Laurent normalization, source support, or
+theorem case. There is otherwise `NO_NEW_MECHANISM`; do not rerun K16's
+anti-invariant norm/DF reformulation.
+
+## Execution and systems
+
+STOP all 99 frontier solves, expansions, retries and numerical witness work;
+retain them only as method controls. REDESIGN D108 around the card before any
+port or compute. REDESIGN K16 toward one uniform obstruction to
+`b*B_m*eta_m!=0`, with the separate `b=0` boundary; retain `(T)` only for
+`t<=8`. CONTINUE structural `u_s=1` receivers and exact source interfaces, but
+stop generic atlas requests without a proposed map. Continue only the already
+authorized bounded parser-overflow/import repair and tiny W190 validation; caps
+on `.63/.73` stay, `.103` stays protected.
+
+Software test (no edit now): a scratch four-case regression keeping theorem
+fields separate—99/66 `GGHV_CLOSED`, 72/108 `GGHV_EXCEPTION`, max 125
+`OUT_OF_SCOPE`, and 99/66 still `GCD_GATE_PASS`—so
+`NOT_CLOSED_BY_THIS_GATE` cannot be mistaken for openness.
+
+Campaign systems: **NO_UPGRADE**. Cleanup satisfies the 48-hour trial. A dual
+heading index is lower value than pre-launch frontier/literature reconciliation;
